  <DataPropertyAssertion><DataProperty abbreviatedIRI="kt:description"/><NamedIndividual abbreviatedIRI="kt:rf-merge-polarity-inverse-functional"/><Literal>Reduced fuzz seed 101348: r inverse functional, r(a,x0), r(x6,x0) and A(x6) force a = x6, a further NN-rule merge makes a = b, so a, b and x6 are in A. The instance test merged the node of a (with A) into the node of b that had the test concept not A; the merge copied the concepts by their tag only and skipped A because the tag was already there (negated), so the clash was missed and even the asserted x6 : A was lost (fixed: a concept with the opposite polarity is copied as well and clashes, dd53ed1b).</Literal></DataPropertyAssertion>
